        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Israel and Hezbollah trade fire, as US-Iran talks begin in Switzerland Middle East Issued on: 21/06/2026 - 12:08 The Iranian Revolutionary Guards declared the Strait of Hormuz shut again on Saturday. Meanwhile Iranian state media says high level officials have arrived in Switzerland for peace talks starting this Sunday. And after initially cancelling his trip, US Vice President JD Vance has landed to take part. Tehran's nuclear programme and other points in the agreement are conditional on a halt in fighting in Lebanon. But the Lebanese civil defence said 20 people were killed by Israeli strikes on Saturday. Details from the ground by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Tehran and Beirut, Reza Sayah and Renée Davis. Iran claims Lebanon 'main topic' at peace talks with US 21/06/2026 Middle East US-Iran peace talks to begin, after Tehran closed Strait of Hormuz 21/06/2026 Middle East Iran closes Strait of Hormuz despite ceasefire after continued Israeli strikes in Lebanon 20/06/2026 Middle East Israel strikes Lebanon despite ceasefire, at least 16 killed 20/06/2026 Middle East NGOs in Lebanon denounce Israeli attacks on medics amid ceasefire 20/06/2026 Middle East Could Israel lose Donald Trump’s support by continuing to drop bombs in Lebanon? 20/06/2026 Middle East Hezbollah-Israel flare-up in Lebanon despite ceasefire announced by the USA 20/06/2026 Middle East US-Iran ceasefire negociations underway in Switzerland 20/06/2026 Middle East Residents flee as Israeli strikes target southern Lebanon 20/06/2026 Middle East"
